TEST-001 class-wide fix -- kill verification
Generated 2026-08-08, sdd-forge-wt-phase4 worktree, branch feature/wave9-design-sync.

## Background

QG cycle-2 evaluator finding (T-001 re-review, seq0569): the cycle-2 Major
fix landed a Values-cell-only exact-match check for TEST-001 (AG_VALUES_NORM
must equal exactly "`standing` | `per-feature` | `off`"). AC-001
(requirements.md :29) requires "no fourth value is described anywhere in
the definition", which is broader than that one table cell. Two mutants
demonstrate the gap:

  - M6: a fourth branch definition appended to the key row's own Meaning
    cell -- "`auto`: let the agent decide per upload without asking."
    (mirrors the row's three legitimate `per-feature`:/`standing`:/`off`:
    branch definitions, just for an undefined fourth value).
  - M7: a new sentence appended to the section's own intro paragraph,
    ahead of the table -- "Some keys also accept `auto`, a fourth value
    ..." -- naming a fourth value without ever touching the Values cell.

Both mutants leave AG_VALUES_NORM untouched, so the round-1/cycle-2 check
alone does not see either of them.

## Fix

Added a further required clause to TEST-001 (both runtimes), on top of the
pre-existing Values-cell exact-match and hedge-word checks (both kept
unchanged): AG_PS_BRANCH_TOKENS (.sh) / $agPsBranchTokensMatch (.ps1) --
the set of backtick-quoted literals occurring in "branch-defining"
position across the section's own intro paragraph plus the setting's own
key row (deliberately excluding the table's header/separator rows, whose
"Values"/"Default" column names would otherwise read as spurious nearby
"value" prose) -- must equal exactly {standing, per-feature, off}, no more,
no fewer, in either position. A literal counts as branch-defining in
either of two shapes: immediately followed by ':' (the Meaning cell's own
branch-definition shape, catches M6), or immediately followed by ',' with
the word "value"/"values" appearing before the next backtick (the shape a
prose sentence introducing an additional named value naturally takes,
catches M7). Extracted literals are case-folded to lowercase before the
set comparison (this layer's job is only to catch a wholly new branch
name, not AC-031's separate case-sensitivity rule tested elsewhere;
case-folding also correctly resolves the intro's own legitimate
`Standing` case-variant illustration to the real `standing` value).

Files touched: tests/design-sync-standing-consent.tests.sh (TEST-001 block
+ new AG_PS_INTRO_SECTION/AG_PS_INTRO_FLAT/AG_PS_ROW_SCAN/
AG_PS_COLON_TOKENS/AG_PS_COMMA_VALUE_TOKENS/AG_PS_BRANCH_TOKENS/
AG_PS_BRANCH_TOKENS_EXPECTED setup variables) and
tests/design-sync-standing-consent.tests.ps1 (TEST-001 block + new
Get-AllLeftmostMatches/Get-BacktickToken helper functions + mirrored
$agPsIntroLines/$agPsIntroFlat/$agPsRowScan/$agPsColonMatches/
$agPsCommaValueMatches/$agPsBranchTokens/$agPsBranchTokensExpected/
$agPsBranchTokensMatch setup variables). No other file touched.

Note on the .ps1 helper: this file's own header comment states "[regex]
static methods ... are used [nowhere] in this file". Get-AllLeftmostMatches
respects that -- it extracts every non-overlapping leftmost match by
repeated -cmatch/-match + .IndexOf()/.Substring() instead of
[regex]::Matches, safe here because none of this suite's patterns use
lookaround (a match's text is a pure function of the match itself).

